@startuml ComponentDiagram
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title Main components of the system, representing the 4 subfolders. Component Diagram: Overview of core subsystems.

component Administration {
  component Command
  component Controller
  component Dashboard
  component DependencyInjection
  component Events
  component Framework
  component Migration
  component Notification
  component Resources
  component Service
  component Snippet
  component System
}
note right of Administration
  Backend management interface (commands, controllers, dashboard, notifications, etc.)
end note

  ' notes for each Administration subcomponent
note right of Command : CLI commands for administrative tasks
note right of Controller : HTTP controllers for admin interfaces
note right of Dashboard : UI panels for monitoring and management
note right of DependencyInjection : Service definitions and wiring
note right of Events : Event handlers for administration workflows
note right of Framework : Shared utilities for admin modules
note right of Migration : Database migrations for admin features
note right of Notification : Alerts and notification mechanisms
note right of Resources : Templates, assets, and static resources
note right of Service : Core business logic for administrative tasks
note right of Snippet : Reusable template snippets in the admin UI
note right of System : System-level utilities and health checks

component Core {
  component Checkout
  component Content
  component DevOps
  component Framework
  component Installer
  component Maintenance
  component Migration
  component Profiling
  component Service
  component System
  component Test
}
note right of Core
  Fundamental business logic and services (checkout, content, system, etc.)
end note

  ' notes for each Core subcomponent
note right of Checkout : Core checkout processes and payment handling
note right of Content : Content management and rendering services
note right of DevOps : DevOps tooling and system automation
note right of Framework : Core framework utilities and abstractions
note right of Installer : Installation and setup routines
note right of Maintenance : Scheduled maintenance and cleanup tasks
note right of Migration : Core database migrations
note right of Profiling : Performance profiling and analysis tools
note right of Service : Core business logic services
note right of System : System utilities and health checks
note right of Test : Core testing utilities and infrastructure

component Elasticsearch {
  component Admin
  component DependencyInjection
  component Event
  component Framework
  component Migration
  component Product
  component Profiler
  component Resources
  component Sort
  component Test
}
note right of Elasticsearch
  Search backend integration (indices, product data, sorting, profiling, etc.)
end note

  ' notes for each Elasticsearch subcomponent
note right of Admin : Elasticsearch index administration and config
note right of DependencyInjection : DI configuration for search integration
note right of Event : Elasticsearch-specific event listeners
note right of Framework : Shared framework utilities for search modules
note right of Migration : Elasticsearch index migrations and upgrades
note right of Product : Product indexing and search model definitions
note right of Profiler : Query profiling integration with Elasticsearch
note right of Resources : Resource definitions for search assets
note right of Sort : Sorting algorithms and ranking criteria
note right of Test : Testing utilities and fixtures for search backend

component Storefront {
  component Checkout
  component Controller
  component DependencyInjection
  component Event
  component Framework
  component Migration
  component Page
  component Pagelet
  component Resources
  component Test
  component Theme
}
note right of Storefront
  Public-facing UI and page rendering (controllers, pages, themes, checkout, etc.)
end note

  ' notes for each Storefront subcomponent
note right of Checkout : Storefront checkout UI and workflow
note right of Controller : HTTP controllers for storefront pages
note right of DependencyInjection : DI configuration for storefront modules
note right of Event : Storefront event listeners and dispatchers
note right of Framework : Shared frontend framework abstractions
note right of Migration : Storefront database migrations
note right of Page : Page controllers and templates
note right of Pagelet : Reusable UI components (pagelets)
note right of Resources : Static assets and templates for storefront
note right of Test : Frontend and integration testing utilities
note right of Theme : Theming and styling configurations

legend right
  |== Component ==| Root level subsystems |
  |-- Subcomponent --| Direct subfolders |
endlegend

@enduml
